WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.850
84-453-3-7-8 Asugaya-nantou,
Suginami-ku, Tokyo
 To: Mori Luou c/o Godai 
Home hinemosu 3-chome, 
Kuragamauji, Kanagawa

00:00:01.790 --> 00:00:04.850
In exchange for arranging for you 
to enter overseas competitions,

00:00:04.850 --> 00:00:06.610
I gave you two conditions:

00:00:06.610 --> 00:00:12.110
go to school and win MVP 
at the ballet festival.

00:00:12.110 --> 00:00:14.440
To do that, you need 
to participate in lesso—

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.490
I...

00:00:15.490 --> 00:00:19.010
don't think I can study 
under you, after all.

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.370
I can't bear to stand on the 
same stage as that wild monkey.

00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.520
<i>He</i> wants to be a Bolshoi 
or Mariinsky danseur noble?

00:00:27.950 --> 00:00:29.260
How ridiculous!

00:00:29.640 --> 00:00:31.900
Why did you dance in the gym?

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.570
It's amazing, you know?

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:35.910
You've got like, a fan club now,

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:38.410
and the video from it is super popular.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:40.890
Everything changed 
because of that whole thing!

00:00:40.890 --> 00:00:42.400
Nothing's changed.

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:48.110
Those guys lost interest in me 
because you distracted them.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:49.170
What?!

00:00:49.410 --> 00:00:51.050
That's not it!

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:52.650
That's not it at all!

00:00:53.410 --> 00:00:56.230
Your dancing actually reached them, too!

00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:01.180
At least, I was able to 
tell them back then...

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.550
and I'm here right now because...

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:09.210
Because when you danced, 
it ended up changing my life!

00:01:10.190 --> 00:01:13.050
That's why, you bastard...

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:17.050
In other words, um...

00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.050
Thanks.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.410
Anyway, I said what I wanted to say,

00:01:25.410 --> 00:01:26.640
so I'm gonna go now!

00:01:28.190 --> 00:01:30.110
Oh, one more thing.

00:01:30.630 --> 00:01:34.610
It's true that I'm a wild 
monkey compared to you,

00:01:34.610 --> 00:01:37.110
and I'm knee-deep in basic training.

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:39.240
But you know,

00:01:40.310 --> 00:01:42.240
while you keep hiding in your room,

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.500
I'm gonna get better than you.

00:03:19.170 --> 00:03:24.140
Act 5: "I Can't Die Now"

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:24.600
In the second half of <i>Swan Lake</i>,

00:03:25.090 --> 00:03:27.510
Prince Siegfried is tricked 
by the demon Rothbart

00:03:27.510 --> 00:03:31.260
and betrays Princess Odette.

00:03:31.260 --> 00:03:33.730
He goes to the lake to apologize,

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:37.670
and the princess forgives him even 
as the other swans try to stop her.

00:03:38.110 --> 00:03:43.510
Then Rothbart creates a storm 
and comes to kill the prince.

00:03:43.510 --> 00:03:47.600
Princess Odette can't go back 
to her original form

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:49.450
and throws herself into the lake,

00:03:49.450 --> 00:03:51.100
so the prince kills himself to follow her.

00:03:51.100 --> 00:03:52.410
What?

00:03:52.410 --> 00:03:56.750
But because of their love, Rothbart dies!

00:03:56.750 --> 00:03:58.300
He was fine a minute ago, though!

00:03:58.300 --> 00:04:03.300
And then the two lovers lived happily 
ever after in the next world. Clap, clap.

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.550
What?!

00:04:04.550 --> 00:04:05.800
Shh!

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:09.500
<i>Swan Lake</i> has a lot of different endings.

00:04:09.500 --> 00:04:13.210
And the version we're doing is different 
from what other studios are doing.

00:04:13.210 --> 00:04:14.810
That's not what I'm surprised about!

00:04:14.810 --> 00:04:17.910
Is it really okay for <i>Swan Lake</i> 
to have such a dumb story?!

00:04:17.910 --> 00:04:19.280
Shh!

00:04:19.280 --> 00:04:21.820
Hey, quiet down during rehearsal!

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.070
<b>Zeneon Suginami</b>

00:04:22.570 --> 00:04:26.070
73rd Suginami 
<b>Ballet Festival</b>

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:34.180
Oh, Natsuki-chan?

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.810
You're here!

00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:37.830
Yeah.

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:44.090
Are you okay?

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:44.720
Sorry!

00:04:44.720 --> 00:04:48.980
Wow... This totally feels 
like a school recital.

00:04:50.050 --> 00:04:53.270
<i>Next is the Godai Ballet Studio.</i>

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.940
<i>Go ahead.</i>

00:04:59.630 --> 00:05:02.860
<i>In the ending of our version of </i>Swan Lake<i>,</i>

00:05:02.860 --> 00:05:05.720
<i>the instant the prince rushes in...</i>

00:05:05.720 --> 00:05:07.360
Jumpei, don't stomp around like that!

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:12.950
<i>The princess is killed in front of his eyes 
by Rothbart, played by Luou.</i>

00:05:13.360 --> 00:05:14.430
<i>And then,</i>

00:05:14.430 --> 00:05:16.770
<i>the prince and Rothbart fight...</i>

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:19.280
Jumpei, pull harder!

00:05:19.280 --> 00:05:20.380
<i>And fight...</i>

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:22.210
Your fingers!

00:05:22.210 --> 00:05:23.390
Your toes!

00:05:23.390 --> 00:05:24.710
Your knees!

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:28.390
<i>But the prince loses in no time.</i>

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:35.760
<i>He takes the princess's hand,</i>

00:05:36.230 --> 00:05:39.660
<i>and they're swallowed up by the stormy lake.</i>

00:05:43.530 --> 00:05:46.650
<b>Godai Ballet Studio
 Dressing Room</b>

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.400
Hey.

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:46.650
Isn't this dumb?

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.940
Doesn't it turn into a school recital 
when I get on stage?

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.540
It's already a dumb story,

00:05:55.010 --> 00:05:57.130
but isn't this just torturing the audience?

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.150
"Audience," huh?

00:05:59.150 --> 00:06:00.540
What?

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:07.030
Well, there are a lot of ballets with
 stories that make you go, "Huh?"

00:06:08.480 --> 00:06:14.180
But the dancers get into character and
 dig deep to make them interesting.

00:06:14.690 --> 00:06:17.710
That's why, even if you can describe 
<i>Swan Lake</i> in a sentence or two,

00:06:18.050 --> 00:06:21.530
with the number of dancers 
and directors there are

00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:25.070
and how you can combine them, 
it can be staged in infinite ways.

00:06:28.010 --> 00:06:31.350
In addition, since these 
performances are live,

00:06:31.350 --> 00:06:34.370
even if the same person performs 
under the same conditions,

00:06:34.370 --> 00:06:37.430
no two performances 
will be exactly the same.

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:41.750
My top half will be <i>Barry Lyndon</i>!

00:06:42.300 --> 00:06:45.380
My bottom half will be <i>A Clockwork Orange</i>!

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:49.420
I'm head-to-toe Stanley Kubrick!

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:50.710
If I think about it that way,

00:06:50.710 --> 00:06:53.390
I could even call this costume cool!

00:06:53.860 --> 00:06:58.600
So part of getting into character 
is finding similarities within yourself?

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:01.150
You watch a lot of movies, huh?

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.150
Well, I'm sure you can give an interesting 
performance with your acting.

00:07:07.280 --> 00:07:08.280
That said!

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.400
You're not at that point yet!

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:11.280
R-R-Right!

00:07:11.700 --> 00:07:14.130
No matter how in-character you are,

00:07:14.130 --> 00:07:19.160
at your age, people will notice if you 
neglect the basics, and that'll spoil it.

00:07:19.810 --> 00:07:23.730
Then it really <i>will</i> be worse than
 a school recital. Unthinkable!

00:07:25.630 --> 00:07:28.750
I'll do... my best...

00:07:28.750 --> 00:07:31.920
Okay, everyone! I'm going to take 
a group picture, so gather together!

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:33.470
Okay!

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:37.310
Hey, didn't I say no snacking 
with your costume on?

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:39.160
I just fixed your makeup!

00:07:38.410 --> 00:07:39.810
I want one!

00:07:40.680 --> 00:07:44.240
It's amazing that he looks so good in that!

00:07:41.110 --> 00:07:45.190
<i>This guy's right out of </i>The Dark Knight<i>!</i>

00:07:45.190 --> 00:07:48.810
No fair! I wanna be the Dark Knight!

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:48.390
Look this way!

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.280
Okay!

00:07:48.810 --> 00:07:50.180
Be quiet.

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:52.320
Say cheese!

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:54.220
Okay, that's enough.

00:07:58.070 --> 00:08:01.200
Everyone, it's almost time to take the stage.

00:08:02.980 --> 00:08:07.880
You've all practiced really, really hard.

00:08:09.340 --> 00:08:14.150
You worked so very hard, 
and you've all improved drastically.

00:08:16.050 --> 00:08:20.530
I'm incredibly proud of all of you.

00:08:22.050 --> 00:08:28.730
This is the last time you'll be able to 
dance this <i>Swan Lake</i> with this group.

00:08:31.740 --> 00:08:32.740
So...

00:08:33.380 --> 00:08:35.780
Go out there and have fun!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:37.400
Okay!

00:08:41.610 --> 00:08:43.300
<i>Oh, yeah...</i>

00:08:44.180 --> 00:08:45.760
<i>This is the last time...</i>

00:08:48.720 --> 00:08:50.330
Sorry.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.410
Miyako?

00:08:51.890 --> 00:08:52.790
What's wrong?

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:58.510
If I look down, my tears will fall 
and mess up my makeup...

00:08:58.510 --> 00:09:01.810
What? Just from Chizuru-san's little pep talk?

00:09:08.210 --> 00:09:10.150
Come on, let's go.

00:09:11.280 --> 00:09:14.530
Thanks. You're such a prince!

00:09:19.530 --> 00:09:24.160
<i>I guess this is the last time 
I'll be Miyako's prince, too.</i>

00:09:24.160 --> 00:09:25.870
Stairs coming up.

00:09:25.870 --> 00:09:27.000
Okay.

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:37.510
At first,

00:09:38.240 --> 00:09:42.770
I didn't think you fit the image of a prince.

00:09:42.770 --> 00:09:44.770
Huh? Yeah, I figured.

00:09:44.770 --> 00:09:48.180
But your prince still had 
the essence of royalty

00:09:48.180 --> 00:09:50.020
while being new and interesting!

00:09:50.460 --> 00:09:53.460
Liar. It weirded you out, didn't it?

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.740
That was, well...

00:10:00.070 --> 00:10:04.450
I mean, I know that it's acting.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:05.290
Huh?

00:10:06.270 --> 00:10:09.470
I know that, but...

00:10:10.040 --> 00:10:17.740
It was the first time a boy 
looked at me so earnestly.

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:22.430
<i>I was just surprised...</i>

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.690
D-Don't look at me!

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:31.160
<i>I-I can't tell!</i>

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:35.370
<i>She's got such heavy makeup on, 
but she looks embarrassed...</i>

00:10:36.370 --> 00:10:40.160
<i>Am I missing something important right now?</i>

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:41.550
Onee-chan!

00:10:41.550 --> 00:10:43.690
Oh, coming!

00:10:45.010 --> 00:10:46.910
H-Hey...

00:10:48.660 --> 00:10:51.070
I-I'll do my best.

00:10:54.290 --> 00:10:56.850
Yeah, let's have fun.

00:10:58.150 --> 00:11:01.260
See you on stage, Prince.

00:11:03.990 --> 00:11:11.060
<i>Next is the Takara Ballet Studio 
performing Act 4 of </i>Swan Lake<i>.</i>

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:24.830
Luou, I was a little worried that you 
weren't actually going to perform.

00:11:28.120 --> 00:11:30.990
I'm gonna get better than you.

00:11:36.410 --> 00:11:39.880
As promised, if you get MVP today,

00:11:39.880 --> 00:11:42.840
I'll arrange for you to compete 
in overseas competitions.

00:11:43.320 --> 00:11:45.980
It should be a piece of cake for you, right?

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.600
<b>Zeneon Suginami</b>

00:11:47.100 --> 00:11:49.600
73rd Suginami 
<b>Ballet Festival</b>

00:11:49.050 --> 00:11:52.230
Come on, Jumpei's studio 
is about to go on!

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.810
Screw this.

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:01.860
I was gonna make fun of him, 
but it's just a pain now.

00:12:02.440 --> 00:12:03.530
Idiot!

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:06.320
What do you mean? You even
 skipped training camp to come!

00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:07.390
H-Hey—

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:23.300
What the hell's he wearing?

00:12:23.770 --> 00:12:25.140
Shh!

00:12:25.140 --> 00:12:27.640
I can't believe it. It's like he lost a bet.

00:12:47.370 --> 00:12:48.530
"I love you."

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:50.500
You can almost hear him saying it.

00:12:50.500 --> 00:12:52.790
Yes, you really can!

00:12:52.790 --> 00:12:55.540
Jumpei-kun's completely different 
from the dress rehearsal.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:57.790
He's like a different 
person! It's wonderful!

00:12:58.140 --> 00:12:59.620
Really?

00:12:59.620 --> 00:13:03.860
He's not paying attention to any of the basics 
Chizuru-sensei warned him about.

00:13:03.860 --> 00:13:05.300
It's hard to watch.

00:13:05.690 --> 00:13:10.290
Someone with a trained eye would
 think the studio's standards are low.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:12.450
That's Yuria-chan's mom for you!

00:13:12.450 --> 00:13:15.140
You used to study ballet, didn't you?

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:16.940
And compared to him... Look.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:27.230
Luou-kun's on a completely different level.

00:13:27.230 --> 00:13:28.180
You're right!

00:13:28.180 --> 00:13:29.320
He is!

00:13:30.010 --> 00:13:32.980
No matter how you look at it, 
Luou-kun is the MVP.

00:13:34.210 --> 00:13:36.370
<i>I guess he really is amazing.</i>

00:13:36.910 --> 00:13:39.260
<i>But even more than Jumpei,</i>

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.250
<i>he's the one who looks like 
a different person.</i>

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:48.260
Maybe it's just because I don't
 know much about ballet,

00:13:48.850 --> 00:13:53.830
but when Jumpei-kun comes out, 
it's kind of exciting, in a way.

00:14:08.110 --> 00:14:12.560
Jumpei! You're not paying attention 
to anything I told you!

00:14:12.560 --> 00:14:14.630
The basics are more important 
than the acting!

00:14:16.040 --> 00:14:17.620
You're not listening, are you?

00:14:18.120 --> 00:14:20.880
<i>C'mon! I wanna go!</i>

00:14:21.770 --> 00:14:23.680
<i>I wanna go out there!</i>

00:14:24.380 --> 00:14:28.380
Okay, fine. At least go and die gracefully.

00:14:28.380 --> 00:14:30.890
<i>I belong out there!</i>

00:14:30.890 --> 00:14:31.950
<i>Come on...</i>

00:14:32.450 --> 00:14:33.560
<i>Come on!</i>

00:14:46.310 --> 00:14:47.770
<i>Odette!</i>

00:14:47.770 --> 00:14:49.700
<i>Where are you, Odette?!</i>

00:14:56.690 --> 00:14:59.120
Everyone's focused on Jumpei now!

00:15:01.230 --> 00:15:02.590
<i>I'm excited...</i>

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:10.580
<i>Odette!</i>

00:15:11.130 --> 00:15:16.350
<i>The first girl I chose myself, 
disobeying the queen!</i>

00:15:18.530 --> 00:15:19.750
<i>And yet...</i>

00:15:21.240 --> 00:15:26.190
<i>How powerless and foolish I am!</i>

00:16:03.400 --> 00:16:09.820
<i>Oh, I wanted to at least be faithful to you.</i>

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:19.090
<i>So even death will be a rite that
 makes a moment with you eternal.</i>

00:16:21.690 --> 00:16:23.570
<i>Odette...</i>

00:16:23.570 --> 00:16:24.980
<i>I'm sorry...</i>

00:16:27.380 --> 00:16:28.880
Prince.

00:16:31.150 --> 00:16:39.110
It was the first time a boy 
looked at me so earnestly.

00:16:40.150 --> 00:16:45.000
<i>My... first girl!</i>

00:16:47.690 --> 00:16:50.340
Okay, little swans.

00:16:50.340 --> 00:16:54.780
Cover up the prince and
 princess, and do your dance.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.030
Okay.

00:16:56.030 --> 00:16:57.910
But Sensei,

00:16:57.910 --> 00:17:00.540
the prince came back to life!

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:05.420
I can't...

00:17:06.510 --> 00:17:08.450
die now!

00:17:15.950 --> 00:17:17.930
Why did Jumpei-kun stand back up?!

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:24.640
<i>Why is the monkey coming back to life?</i>

00:17:25.950 --> 00:17:27.730
<i>What is he thinking?</i>

00:17:29.720 --> 00:17:32.940
Kill... him... now!

00:17:33.460 --> 00:17:35.080
<i>This is why...</i>

00:17:35.080 --> 00:17:38.210
<i>I didn't want to stand on the same 
stage with someone like him!</i>

00:17:40.310 --> 00:17:41.160
That surprised me!

00:17:41.160 --> 00:17:43.910
Boys' ballet is really powerful...

00:17:48.480 --> 00:17:49.750
The next time I throw you,

00:17:50.360 --> 00:17:51.380
make sure you die!

00:17:53.670 --> 00:17:54.300
<i>Hey!</i>

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.710
<i>Die!</i>

00:17:58.590 --> 00:17:59.930
Jumpei jumped higher!

00:17:59.930 --> 00:18:02.550
Higher doesn't mean better.

00:18:03.490 --> 00:18:05.140
<i>Stop messing around!</i>

00:18:06.390 --> 00:18:08.060
<i>I'm better than you!</i>

00:18:09.080 --> 00:18:12.660
<i>I'll defeat you, completely and utterly!</i>

00:18:13.430 --> 00:18:15.040
Rothbart's so fast!

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:16.400
He's catching up to the prince!

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:28.550
Behind him!

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:36.590
<i>Why is he getting in my way?</i>

00:18:38.560 --> 00:18:39.590
What?

00:18:39.590 --> 00:18:43.360
What's going on? The song's about to end!

00:18:43.750 --> 00:18:46.480
I'm not satisfied ye—

00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:50.850
<i>Oh.</i>

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:52.770
<i>This...</i>

00:18:53.610 --> 00:18:55.770
<i>In front of me...</i>

00:18:56.610 --> 00:19:06.120
<i>is a pure, endless embodiment of
 loathing that won't listen to reason...</i>

00:19:07.940 --> 00:19:09.000
That's...

00:19:09.830 --> 00:19:11.110
a demon...

00:19:12.810 --> 00:19:14.590
<i>I can't win!</i>

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:25.350
<i>Serves you right.</i>

00:19:26.120 --> 00:19:27.890
<i>Serves you right!</i>

00:19:28.150 --> 00:19:29.890
<i>You, and you,</i>

00:19:29.890 --> 00:19:32.830
<i>and you and you and you and you and you!</i>

00:20:31.120 --> 00:20:32.630
Amazing!

00:20:32.630 --> 00:20:34.960
That was fun!

00:20:40.600 --> 00:20:43.580
I'm not sure what happened, 
but that was amazing, huh?

00:20:55.410 --> 00:20:57.120
<i>What...</i>

00:20:57.120 --> 00:20:59.840
<i>Who am I?</i>

00:21:00.640 --> 00:21:02.190
<i>What was I doing?</i>

00:21:02.190 --> 00:21:03.430
Luou.

00:21:06.930 --> 00:21:09.430
Good job getting through that...

00:21:10.880 --> 00:21:12.890
as Rothbart!

00:21:19.480 --> 00:21:20.480
On the other hand...

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:22.710
Jumpei, you—

00:21:23.900 --> 00:21:25.220
Crap...

00:21:26.350 --> 00:21:29.000
I had <i>so</i> much fun...

00:21:31.970 --> 00:21:37.480
Encore! Encore!

00:21:33.050 --> 00:21:33.930
Hey!

00:21:33.930 --> 00:21:35.140
Wow!

00:21:35.140 --> 00:21:37.480
Hey, isn't this amazing? An encore!

00:21:37.480 --> 00:21:47.490
Encore! Encore!

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:50.120
What? An encore?

00:21:47.490 --> 00:21:56.990
Encore! Encore!

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.480
This is the first time in 
the history of the festival.

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:55.500
<b>Oikawa Ayako</b>

00:21:54.500 --> 00:21:58.620
Really, it is unprecedented...

00:22:01.480 --> 00:22:03.690
to have such a lowbrow performance.

00:23:34.890 --> 00:23:35.890
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:36.240 --> 00:23:39.130
That glittering "bang" was amazing!

00:23:39.610 --> 00:23:42.480
But if that's not ballet...

00:23:43.250 --> 00:23:47.970
<i>Dance Dance Danseur</i>, Act 6: 
"Why Am I Doing Ballet?"

00:23:45.730 --> 00:23:49.990
Act 6 
"Why Am I Doing Ballet?"
